Market shocks, regulatory surprises and leadership gaps tend to cluster. Organizations that cope well have usually rehearsed the first 72 hours in advance.

## Pre-Agree Decision Rights

Ambiguity about who can approve what is the most common cause of delay in a crisis. A short, board-approved matrix of emergency authorities removes it.

## Rehearse Quarterly

A 90-minute tabletop exercise each quarter keeps the plan current and surfaces gaps while the stakes are low.
